# Configuration

## Framework semantics

App config lives under `config/` (`app.php`, `app_local.php`, etc.). CakePHP 5 supports a PSR container via `Application::services()` for wiring dependencies. Prefer config + container over scattered `new` of infrastructure in controllers.

## Required behavior

- Keep secrets and environment-specific values in config/`app_local` / env — not hardcoded in domain classes.
- Register shared infrastructure in `Application::services()` when the project already uses DI.
- Do not invent Laravel ServiceProvider / facades as CakePHP defaults.
- Prefer CakePHP Configure / config files for feature flags and connection settings.

## Anti-patterns

- Hardcoding credentials or hostnames in controllers/Tables
- Inventing ServiceProvider / facade layers
- New container abstractions that bypass Application services without cause

## Review checklist

- [ ] Env-specific values come from config/env
- [ ] Shared services follow project DI patterns
- [ ] No Laravel provider mental model
